WEBVTT

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.980
<b>Fall Couples</b>

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.980
<b>Special
Date Issue</b>

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.940
Good work today.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.560
Um, you wanted to see me?

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.320
<b>Arks</b>

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.320
<b>Fan Festa</b>

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.900
Tachibana-kun, do you...

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.720
...have any plans for this weekend?

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.690
Not really.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.960
If you're free, um...

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.180
There's something I want you to do.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.620
Is it a student council job?

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.720
W-Well, I suppose you could call it that.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.220
It's, well...

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.850
There's somewhere I want you to go with me.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.480
<b>Special
Date Issue</b>

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:51.980
<b>Special
Date Issue</b>

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.360
<b>Special
Date Issue</b>

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.820
<i>I-Is this...</i>

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:03.030
Hey, Itsuki. You're going to 
the thing this weekend, right?

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.260
This weekend?

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.750
Let's go together.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:09.270
It's a big event that 
only happens once a year.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.600
Sorry, Kota.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:19.530
Unfortunately, I've already got plans for that day.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.140
Ask someone else.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.280
What?

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:58.360
<b>Quest 04      Phantasy Star Offline</b>

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:05.780
<b>ARKS Fan Festa</b>

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.790
What... is this?

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.290
The ARKS Fan Festa.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.300
It's an annual <i>PSO2</i> fan event.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.300
An event?

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:23.460
It's an opportunity to get closer
 in the real world

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:26.330
to friends you normally only meet online

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:30.560
and learn more about the world of <i>PSO2</i>.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:32.560
Um...

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:36.400
So this isn't a date, then.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.080
What? Did you say something?

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.580
N-Nothing!

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.200
An ARKS Card?

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:47.580
Yes. Please enter the character name
 you use in-game.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.200
I see.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.700
This way we'll recognize each other
if we've met in-game.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:55.830
Itsuki

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.810
What's wrong? Let's go inside.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:01.840
Y-Yes, you're right.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.470
Human!

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.850
Newman!

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.220
Hey, Duman!

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:18.860
And CAST!

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.860
All together now!

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.580
Oh, wow!

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.740
I'm starting to get really excited!

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.160
Um...

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.120
Huh? Wh-What?

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:40.590
Is this your first time 
attending this event, too?

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:43.100
S-So what if it is?

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.960
I'm just kind of surprised.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.260
Well...

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.860
You were too busy.

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:53.980
You normally have
 lots of student council work,

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:59.020
so you couldn't take time off
 in order to attend a <i>PSO2</i> event.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.030
W-Well, yeah.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.780
Then let's have a blast today.

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:14.000
All these people play <i>PSO2</i>.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:19.230
The ARKS Fan Festa isn't an official event.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.490
It's entirely organized and 
operated by volunteer groups.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:22.720
I see.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:27.010
It's probably one of the largest
amateur-run events in the nation—

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:34.640
You just thought I have some nerve to talk like
I know it all when it's my first time, didn't you?

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:37.270
I wasn't thinking that at all.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.760
No, you definitely were.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:42.520
You're overthinking this.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:46.680
I won't be able to see everything in one day.

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.110
If only Itsuki had come, too.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:52.630
Itsuki? What's he doing here?

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:55.700
He said he had plans today.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:04.210
Is... Is that Izumi-senpai?

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:06.510
What's she doing with Itsuki?

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:09.880
Unfortunately, I've already got plans for that day.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.510
Ask someone else.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:13.890
Could it be?

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:19.900
There was a mysterious air of superiority
surrounding him that day!

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:25.650
Is this why?!

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:30.600
Huh? I thought I just heard a familiar voice.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.610
She's cute.

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:37.160
Look this way.

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.140
I suppose I stand out in these clothes.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:49.140
I've seen those clothes in-game before.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:54.430
Many people wear costumes identical to
the ones worn by their characters in-game.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.840
It's called in-character cosplay.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:59.940
Wow, it's exactly like in the game.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.620
Hey, it's Itsuki.

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:07.320
What?

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.090
Uh...

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:12.340
Are you talking to me?

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:13.950
It's me.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.020
We've played together a few times.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.450
<b>Silver</b>

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:17.680
Silver...

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:19.460
What?!

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:23.140
Talk about an overreaction.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:25.180
Is it that surprising?

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:28.120
But you look nothing like your character!

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:30.000
I'm Itsuki.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.220
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:33.660
Why are you being so polite 
to a grade school kid?

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.720
But in the game, you're my senior.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.820
This here is...

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:40.920
Wait, what?

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:43.440
Guys, over here!

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.580
Guys?

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:48.820
Nice to meet you.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:49.710
What?

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.990
Yumiko

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:52.120
You're Yumiko-san of the kimono duo?

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:55.870
Hello. I'm Yumiko.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:58.320
How unexpected. How totally unexpected.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.600
That kimono duo is actually a super normal...

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.470
Oh, sorry.

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:05.380
Don't worry about it. We get that lot.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.130
Last Samurai

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:09.130
Then this is Last Samurai-san?

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:12.340
Last Samurai is my husband.

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:15.530
O-Of course.

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:18.000
Nice to make your acquaintance.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.390
Boy, it's embarrassing to 
talk that way in real life.

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.140
And you're...

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.140
Kid

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.060
Kid-san?

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:30.860
I'm Kid. Nice to meet you.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.650
You're totally different, too.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:37.280
I can't believe that hot-blooded hero
is a classy old man.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.880
Quit overreacting already.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:41.310
Sorry.

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:42.540
It's understandable.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:48.140
We were just as surprised
the first time we met you guys offline.

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:51.570
But, Itsuki-san, you look 
exactly like you do in game.

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:53.420
What? Really?

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.920
Yeah. You look pretty similar.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.460
Maybe I'll leave.

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:06.660
Take one.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:08.770
<b>Cosplay Plaza</b>

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:08.770
<b>In-Character Photo Shoot</b>

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:13.620
Thank you!

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:14.950
Say "cheese!"

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.270
Yeah.

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:27.000
You got some on your face.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.290
Itsuki's so lucky.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.820
Of course he chose his date over his bro.

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:38.930
Looks like you've suffered serious damage.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:42.070
Yeah. I've only got one hit point left.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:49.000
Drink this. It should help you recover some.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.060
What?

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.550
Hey, that cosplay is super-realistic.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:57.980
That's way beyond just in-character.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.110
Is this Monomate?

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:16.630
<i>I feel an indescribable strength 
welling up from inside my soul!</i>

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:21.220
Oh, right. I'd better thank her.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:31.140
SORO? As in that genius 
Gunner "Mr. Aloof"?

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:33.350
I had no idea she was so beautiful.

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:34.980
No one can talk to her.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.460
Of course not.

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:41.070
There's practically no way 
anyone could talk to her now.

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:45.190
<i>I've always fought by myself.</i>

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:48.700
<i>I don't need friends now.</i>

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:50.540
<i>But wait...</i>

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:52.980
<i>I can't hit anything!</i>

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:54.800
<i>What's wrong with this thing?</i>

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:58.840
She doesn't seem very approachable...

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:03.220
There you are.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.660
Let's go.

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:12.520
There she is. That's her.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:15.610
Hey! Thanks for earlier.

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.490
Uh, I...

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:19.670
SORO?

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:21.740
You're "Mr. Aloof"?

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:22.530
What?

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:23.920
You're <i>the</i> Mr. Aloof?

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:27.740
Oh, my. I can't believe I'm meeting 
the real Mr. Aloof at an event!

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:32.750
So he's actually a sweet young lady.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.990
I'm getting goosebumps.

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:36.500
Hey, Mr. Aloof.

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:39.000
Let's go questing together sometime.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:43.300
In that case, allow me to join you.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.700
What? No fair.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.140
Let me come, too.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.010
Me, too.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.680
No way. I invited Mr. Aloof first.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:51.770
Right, Mr. Aloof?

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:57.830
But I prefer to play by myself.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:11:59.930
What are you talking about?

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:01.000
What?

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:06.780
Getting closer in the real world to
friends you normally only meet online.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:09.180
Isn't that what the ARKS Fan Festa is about?

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:11.220
Tachibana-kun...

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:17.500
Then let's play together sometime.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:18.450
All right!

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:19.210
What?

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:21.610
I wanted it to be just the two of us.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:25.550
Huh? Where did that girl go?

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:40.360
<b>[Offline Events] A common name for large events where users of online games meet outside the game (in the real world). The term was coined to avoid confusion with in-game and online events held for all players.</b>

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:44.950
<b>[Monomate] A healing item used to recover a player character's HP in <i>PSO2</i>. A single use heals up to 30% HP. This beverage-type healing tonic is consumed orally. All species use the same method of consumption, including CASTs, though how exactly they consume it will likely be a mystery forever.</b>

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:51.420
What? Itsuki's your real name?

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:53.790
Is that bad?

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.340
It's not <i>bad</i>, but...

00:12:58.190 --> 00:13:00.020
Not many people do that.

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:02.330
Most people don't use their real name.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:04.570
I just didn't know.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:07.260
You didn't tell me, either.

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.300
What? I didn't?

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:11.730
You didn't tell me anything.

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.720
You have food on your face.

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:20.940
Are they an item?

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:25.950
Uh, what's going on?

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:34.210
I hate to be presumptuous, but I'd 
like to ask a question for the group.

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:35.460
Would that be all right?

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:36.470
Okay.

00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:37.260
What is it?

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.540
Are you two—

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:40.860
No!

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:42.590
W-We're not.

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:45.460
They denied it immediately. We're right!

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:47.500
I said we're not!

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:49.320
There's nothing wrong with it if you are.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.010
There's everything wrong with it!

00:13:54.520 --> 00:14:01.980
I-Itsuki

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.400
Koa's calling me?

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.490
Koa? You mean Kayano-kun?

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:06.760
Hey, what's up?

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:11.600
I'm currently participating in the 
same gathering of warriors as you.

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:13.600
Gathering of warriors?

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:17.000
You're here at the ARKS Fan Festa?

00:14:17.110 --> 00:14:20.650
Oh, so this is the weekend event
 you were talking about.

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:23.750
More importantly, we need to talk.

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:25.330
What's wrong?

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:28.770
I'm currently beset by 
unforeseen circumstances.

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:32.010
In pitch darkness, I'm surrounded 
on all sides by callous walls.

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.040
Hey, talk to me in
a language I can understand.

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:35.770
In other words...

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:40.020
Itsuki, I need your help.

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:43.640
What? Hey, what happened?

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:45.530
The truth is...

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:48.900
Hey, is anyone there?

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.510
What? Like who?

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:54.580
Not there. In real life.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:55.700
Oh, right.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:15:00.050
Rina-senpai and my friends are here.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:01.570
I see.

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:04.380
Hey, what's wrong?

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:08.170
I can't go into the details right now.

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:10.700
Why not? Where are you?

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:11.930
This isn't good.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:14.100
Sorry. I'll call you later.

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:15.870
Hey!

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:22.290
What in the world happened to him?

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:25.680
He seemed to be at his wit's end.

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:29.130
He may have gotten involved 
in some kind of incident.

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:32.290
Um...

00:15:34.310 --> 00:15:36.540
I heard a weird rumor before.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:37.360
A rumor?

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:40.850
Weird incidents have been happening, right?

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:43.670
Like empty cars driving out 
of control in the city.

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:45.680
Since around the same time,

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:48.600
more and more people have gone missing.

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:52.600
Are the car and missing persons 
incidents related somehow?

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:55.020
I'm not sure.

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:57.400
Let's contact the event 
organizers or security.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:58.700
Wait.

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:02.950
Kayano-kun said he couldn't 
go into the details.

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:07.940
If someone else finds out about it,
things might get even more dangerous.

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:13.470
In any case, we need to find 
Kota and help him quickly.

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:15.100
I'll help, too.

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.460
So will we.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:18.990
I can't offer much, but I'll 
help in whatever way I can.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.360
Thanks.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.510
Let's split up and look for him.

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:27.930
Find Koa wherever he is in the 
event space and rescue him.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:30.740
That's our current quest.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:40.470
Hey, let's try that way.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:41.060
How's it going, everyone?

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:43.720
We didn't find anything.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:45.380
Neither did we.

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:50.060
The event space is too large 
to find a single person.

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:52.820
Silver-san, is something wrong?

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:55.610
Kid, you go on ahead.

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:57.590
What are you talking about?

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.450
I'm exhausted!

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:02.650
I can't walk any more.

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:04.320
Come on.

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:06.800
I'll carry you.

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:08.570
No, that's lame.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:10.810
I told you to go without me.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:12.460
I can't do that.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:16.460
I can't leave you by yourself.

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:20.460
We just went that way.

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:23.350
No, we went that way earlier.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:27.490
I wish your poor sense of direction 
were limited to the game.

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:29.800
I can't ignore that.

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:33.420
We always get lost while questing
because of your mistakes!

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:34.610
Um...

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:36.230
Go on.

00:17:36.230 --> 00:17:36.990
Shut up.

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:40.160
I won't leave you behind, even if it kills me.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.320
Hey, guys...

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:47.420
Have you forgotten?

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.980
The quest has already begun.

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:54.880
If we don't stick together, 
the entire party will be destroyed.

00:17:58.020 --> 00:18:00.370
Could you not look this way?

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:01.390
Sorry.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:03.060
Thank you.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:05.610
I lost control of myself.

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:06.810
Sorry.

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:09.160
Fine. I'll try a little harder.

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:11.400
That's the spirit.

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:12.690
Guys.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:16.420
Let's think carefully over Koa's words again.

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:20.410
It may be a clue to his location.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:22.910
Koa-san's in here?

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:26.160
He said so himself...

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:31.170
In pitch darkness, I'm surrounded 
on all sides by callous walls.

00:18:31.930 --> 00:18:35.170
This is the only dark place
in the event space.

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:38.330
It's sort of creepy in here.

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:43.440
This is Kota's.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:44.770
Then...

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.930
Mr. Aloof's deduction was right on the mark.

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:50.190
Is Kota nearby?

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:51.730
Is that you, Itsuki?

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:53.160
Koa!

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:54.900
Hang in there.

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:57.090
We're nearby.

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:58.660
It's all right.

00:18:58.660 --> 00:18:59.200
What?

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:03.130
Just leave me.

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:05.500
What are you talking about?

00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:07.040
Don't give up!

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:13.390
We will never abandon you.

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:15.480
Believe in us.

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:18.000
We are your friends!

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:21.840
Friends...

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:24.630
How gallant.

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:25.350
I'm in love.

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:29.900
Um, could you not look at me?

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:33.860
Will you tell us what's up?

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:38.540
I'm actually in...

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:42.860
What? Mr. Aloof is Rina-senpai?

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:45.310
I see.

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:48.490
So you were here together 
on student council business.

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:50.840
I thought it was a date.

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:53.500
Anyway, what happened to you?

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:02.380
Well...

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:06.020
This in-character cosplay chick
gave me a Monomate.

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:09.770
While chasing her down so I 
could thank her, I got lost.

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:14.950
Then my stomach suddenly started to feel bad,

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:17.790
so I ran into a nearby bathroom.

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:21.390
But there wasn't any toilet paper in there.

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:23.150
Boy, was I beat.

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:25.400
Huh?

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:27.610
Shall we go, then?

00:20:27.610 --> 00:20:28.290
Yeah.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:30.530
Let's meet again in <i>PSO2</i>.

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:31.910
Good job, everyone.

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:36.830
What? Are you guys mad about that?

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:40.250
Hello?

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:48.740
I know a lot happened, but we ultimately
got to enjoy the ARKS Fan Festa, right?

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:54.650
Senpai?

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.340
Tachibana-kun,

00:20:56.950 --> 00:21:00.480
thanks for today.

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:03.490
What are you talking about?

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:06.400
Feel free to invite me anytime.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:09.810
Yeah. There's that, too, but...

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:14.340
Today, thanks to you, I—

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:16.000
Hey, Itsuki!

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:21.660
Huh? I thought you left already.

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:24.450
Well, I was feeling better,

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:28.210
and then I got held up taking photos
with girls in cosplay.

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:30.870
Let's go home together.

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:33.130
Is it okay if he joins us?

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:36.680
I don't mind.

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:38.770
And?

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:42.100
Did you find the girl who 
gave you the Monomate?

00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:44.530
I couldn't find her anywhere.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:47.660
I at least wanted to see her face.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:51.840
But I know she's definitely cute.

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:54.470
Keep saying that, and you'll 
upset your stomach again.

00:21:54.470 --> 00:21:56.290
Don't say that.

00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:58.540
I think it's back.

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:41.520
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:41.520 --> 00:24:09.340
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:43.070 --> 00:23:45.580
The festival was received 
with thunderous applause.

00:23:45.580 --> 00:23:50.370
However, tossed about by an 
incongruous fate, my repose was shattered.

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:56.550
And my friend running off to find his own spring,

00:23:56.550 --> 00:23:59.360
pierces the darkness in my heart deeply.

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:03.370
However, my conviction is indestructible!

00:24:03.370 --> 00:24:07.730
The winds of spring, blow my way and bless me!

00:24:07.730 --> 00:24:09.380
I have no idea what you're saying.
